  "reply_text": "Found **one merge-blocking issue** in `share-editing`:\n\n**[P1] View-only shares are allowed to edit — `src/guard.js:12`**\n`share.mask & WRITE === WRITE` is parsed as `share.mask & (WRITE === WRITE)`, so it checks bit `1` (`READ`) instead of `WRITE`.\n\nConfirmed:\n- An unlocked viewer (`mask: READ`) gets `canEdit() === true`.\n- An unlocked write-only share (`mask: WRITE`) gets `0`, incorrectly denying editing.\n\nUse `hasRight(share.mask, WRITE) && !share.locked`, consistent with `canComment`. Add tests for a viewer being denied editing and a WRITE-only share being allowed.\n\nAll six existing tests pass; they miss this because the editor fixture has both READ and WRITE. I reviewed the full diff against `main` and found no other concrete issues. **No files changed.**",
